MSYS2 SETUP
-----------

MSYS2 install supports many configurations. Building OpenOCD for
use with WIndows 10/11 will work best with the URCT environment.

1. Start the MSYS2 UCRT64 (Gold MSYS2 icon)

2. Install the build prerequisites
   
   pacman -S unzip bzip2 base-devel mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-toolchain mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-libusb mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-libusb-compat-git mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-hidapi mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-libftdi

3. There is currently no jimtcl for MSYS2, so we need to build it from
   the submodule, even though it is listed as deprecated. Configure and
   build like this:

   cd path/to/openocd/source
   git submodule update --init
   ./configure --enable-internal-jimtcl
   make

MERGE PROCESS
-------------

The first common ancestor between release-0.12.0-1.1.1 (adi) and main (openocd)
is: 01a797af1

When merging we take care to follow the latest OpenOCD style and go for
a minimal change set.

When copying the AD/MAX config, loaders, etc we simply copy the files
over assuming that they are more current tha anything in OpenOCD.

1. Add the shared_connection field to the ARM data structures
2. Merge any lines that use these fields
3. Copy AD/MAX tcl config and contributed flash loaders
4. Fix any compile/link errors (there were not many)

Once the executable is built, we can test using:

cd path/to/new/openocd/tcl
../src/openocd.exe -f interface/cmsis-dap.cfg -f target/max32690.cfg

It works!